[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: System Requirements
UID: YAAP-SR
DATE: @GIT_COMMIT_DATETIME
PREFIX: SR-

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Introduction

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
This document defines the system requirements for Yet Another Audio Player (Yaap),
a time accurate desktop audio player.
<<<

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Main App

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Format Support

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-001
TITLE: FLAC Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the FLAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-002
TITLE: MP3 Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the MP3 format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-003
TITLE: WAV Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files containing supported PCM audio 
in the WAV container format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-004
TITLE: AAC Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of AAC audio stored in supported audio containers,
including M4A audio files.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-005
TITLE: ALAC Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the ALAC format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-006
TITLE: Ogg Vorbis Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the Vorbis codec
in the Ogg container format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-007
TITLE: Opus Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files encoded in the Opus codec in 
supported containers.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-008
TITLE: AIFF Audio Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback of audio files containing supported PCM audio 
in the AIFF container format.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: General Audio Decoding

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-009
TITLE: Audio Format Identification
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall identify the audio format of an input file using its content or 
format metadata rather then relying solely on its file extension.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-001

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-010
TITLE: Unsupported Audio Formats
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when an audio file cannot be played because its format or
encoding is unsupported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-002

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-011
TITLE: Invalid Audio Files
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report an appropriate error when an audio file cannot be decoded
because its contents are invalid or corrupted.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-002

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Local Audio Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-012
TITLE: Local Audio File Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for a local audio file to be browsed or selected for playback.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-013
TITLE: Local Audio File Playback
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall play a selected local audio file when its format and encoding 
are supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-003

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-014
TITLE: Local File Access Failure
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when a selected local audio file cannot be accessed for 
playback.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-003

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Cloud Provider Support

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-015
TITLE: Cloud Provider Support
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support connecting to Google Drive, iCloud Drive, Dropbox,
and Microsoft OneDrive.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-016
TITLE: Cloud Provider Authentication
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support authenticating with a supported cloud storage provider.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-017
TITLE: Cloud Connection Status
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report whether a cloud storage connection has been established
successfully.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-018
TITLE: Cloud Connection Failure
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report an appropriate error when a connection to a cloud storage
provider cannot be established.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-004

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Remote Audio Files

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-019
TITLE: Remote Audio File Selection
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow for audio files to be browsed or selected for playback
through a connected cloud storage provider.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-020
TITLE: Remote Audio File Playback
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall play a selected remote audio file when its format and encoding are
supported and the file is accessible.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-021
TITLE: Remote File Access Failure
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when a selected remote audio file cannot be retrieved
for playback.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-022
TITLE: Remote Playback Interruption
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report when a remote audio file becomes unavailable during playback
and playback cannot continue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-005

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Quality

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-023
TITLE: Audio Decoding Fidelity
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall decode supported audio files according to their encoding format 
without introducing additional lossy encoding during decoding.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-006

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Position

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-024
TITLE: Playback Position Accuracy
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the current playback position of the active audio track 
available to the user.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-025
TITLE: Playback Position Accuracy
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report the playback position within the specified timing accuracy 
under defined operating conditions.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-007

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-026
TITLE: Elapsed Playback Time
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall report the elapsed playback time of the active audio track, 
corresponding to its current playback position.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-007
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-008

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-027
TITLE: Playback Position Seeking
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to request a playback position within the duration 
of the active audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-028
TITLE: Seek Position Accuracy
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall seek to the requested playback position with the greatest accuracy 
supported by the active audio track and playback pipeline, targeting a maximum 
error of 1 microsecond where supported.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-009

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-029
TITLE: Remaining Playback Time
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall display the estimated remaining playback time of the active audio
track, calculated from its duration and current playback position.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-010

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-030
TITLE: Media Playback Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the currently playing track's available playback information 
accessible through the operating system's media-control interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-031
TITLE: Media Playback Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the currently playing track's metadata accessible through 
the operating system's media-control interface, where supported hby that interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-011

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-032
TITLE: Media Playback Controls
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback control commands received through the operating 
system's media-control interface, where supported by that interface.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-011

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Audio Playback Customization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-033
TITLE: Playback Speed Adjustment
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support the adjustment of the playback speed of the active 
audio track.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-034
TITLE: Playback Speed Range
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback speeds within a range of 0.5x to 2.0x at minimum.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-012

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-035
TITLE: Independent Playback Pitch Adjustment
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support the adjustment of the playback pitch independently of 
playback speed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-036
TITLE: Playback Pitch Range
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support playback pitch changes within a range of ±6 semitones
at minimum.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-013

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-037
TITLE: Playback Volume Adjustment
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall support the adjustment of the playback volume within a range 
of 0% to 150%.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-014

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-038
TITLE: Audio Processing Configuration
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall allow the user to configure each supported audio processing option.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-015

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SR-039
TITLE: Active Playback Customisation Information
STATEMENT: >>>
The system shall make the currently active playback speed, pitch adjustment, 
volume setting and audio processing options available for display to the user.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: UR-016

